# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/

# The eBPF for Windows source tree, cloned here to build contoso_sockops.c against
# its headers. It is Microsoft's repository with its own history and licence -- 1,500
# files that are not ours and would be stale the day after they were committed.
# ebpf/setup.ps1 clones it; ebpf/README.md says so.
ebpf/ebpf-for-windows/

# Runtime output. app.console-exporter.log reached 101 MB overnight when the OTLP
# exporter was still writing to the console, which is the kind of thing that should
# never be in a repository even once.
*.log
*.err

# Collector and probe state: the DPAPI-encrypted cloud credential, the spool, and the
# durable ids. Machine-specific, and one of them is a secret.
state/
*.dat

# Local overrides. appsettings.json ships with every secret null on purpose; this is
# where a real endpoint and key would go, and it must not be committed.
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json

# Compiled eBPF object. build.ps1 regenerates it, and clang embeds the absolute build
# path in the binary -- which on a public repo publishes whoever's home directory it
# was built in.
ebpf/*.o
